1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,560
On many small farms, watering is guesswork.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,132
Too much wastes water and electricity;

3
00:00:08,172 --> 00:00:10,275
too little stresses the crop.

4
00:00:10,315 --> 00:00:14,990
AgroFlow helps a farmer decide when
to irrigate, and how much.

5
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:18,861
Meet Thabo, one of our personas:

6
00:00:18,901 --> 00:00:24,432
a tomato farmer near Mafikeng, with one
field split into two irrigation zones.

7
00:00:24,472 --> 00:00:28,718
He asks for a call back on
the AgroFlow website.

8
00:00:28,758 --> 00:00:33,860
If he mistypes his phone number, the
form tells him straight away.

9
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,588
Naledi, our second persona,
is a field officer.

10
00:00:38,628 --> 00:00:42,016
Telegram tells her a new
enquiry has arrived.

11
00:00:42,056 --> 00:00:48,444
In the Enquiries tab she taps "I'll handle
this", so nobody else calls him too.

12
00:00:48,483 --> 00:00:51,014
After the call, she logs it:

13
00:00:51,054 --> 00:00:52,300
Thabo wants AgroFlow.

14
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,600
She starts onboarding
straight from the enquiry,

15
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:59,600
so Thabo's details are already filled in.

16
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:04,743
She adds his farm and both zones,
with crop, soil and size.

17
00:01:04,783 --> 00:01:11,600
The enquiry then shows he became a farmer, and
the activity log records who did it.

18
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:16,329
To hand over, Naledi shows a QR code.

19
00:01:16,369 --> 00:01:21,044
Thabo scans it and presses Start in
the AgroFlow Telegram bot,

20
00:01:21,084 --> 00:01:26,188
which sends his sign-in email, a
temporary password and the app link.

21
00:01:26,228 --> 00:01:31,760
When he first signs in, the app makes
him choose his own password.

22
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,774
Next, the field kit:

23
00:01:34,814 --> 00:01:39,918
an ESP32 board, a Soil Moisture Sensor, a
temperature and humidity sensor,

24
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:42,490
and a relay for the pump.

25
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:47,633
Naledi registers the kit to Zone 1
and gets a one-time code.

26
00:01:47,673 --> 00:01:51,491
On site, the installer joins
the kit's setup Wi-Fi,

27
00:01:51,531 --> 00:01:57,920
enters the farm Wi-Fi and the code, and
the kit links itself to the zone.

28
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:02,648
In the app, Thabo finishes
each zone's setup.

29
00:02:02,688 --> 00:02:09,933
For the flow rate, he times how long his tap
takes to fill a 500 millilitre bottle.

30
00:02:09,973 --> 00:02:17,218
Then he teaches the sensor his soil, with a wet
and a dry reading on different days.

31
00:02:17,258 --> 00:02:20,217
With each step, the advice gets surer:

32
00:02:20,257 --> 00:02:22,360
from medium to high confidence.

33
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:27,089
Every day, Home shows one action per zone.

34
00:02:27,129 --> 00:02:33,517
Today, Zone 1 needs about 66 minutes of water,
or 996 litres, with high confidence.

35
00:02:33,557 --> 00:02:36,946
"Why am I seeing this?" shows the reasons:

36
00:02:36,986 --> 00:02:42,089
the weather, the crop's stage and
the water left in the soil.

37
00:02:42,129 --> 00:02:44,660
The week ahead plans each day.

38
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:46,817
AgroFlow recommends;

39
00:02:46,857 --> 00:02:47,674
Thabo decides.

40
00:02:47,714 --> 00:02:50,674
He starts a run from the app.

41
00:02:50,714 --> 00:02:56,245
The command reaches the kit over MQTT,
the relay switches the pump on,

42
00:02:56,285 --> 00:02:59,245
and the kit reports the run back.

43
00:02:59,285 --> 00:03:06,102
For safety, the kit never runs the pump for
more than five minutes at a time.

44
00:03:06,142 --> 00:03:09,530
Our website demo shows this
as a visualisation.

45
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:12,544
Then the forecast changes:

46
00:03:12,584 --> 00:03:14,687
24 millimetres of rain tomorrow.

47
00:03:14,727 --> 00:03:21,114
AgroFlow works the plan out again, and Zone
2 no longer needs water on Monday.

48
00:03:21,154 --> 00:03:24,971
If rain covers the crop's
need, it says wait;

49
00:03:25,011 --> 00:03:28,399
if it only helps, it says water less.

50
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:30,970
Thabo also gets a Telegram alert.

51
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:35,269
Reports start with what to do next.

52
00:03:35,309 --> 00:03:41,696
Thabo makes his as a PDF in the app, and
automatic ones arrive on Telegram.

53
00:03:41,736 --> 00:03:47,266
Naledi can preview a farm's report, download
PDF or Excel, and schedule daily,

54
00:03:47,306 --> 00:03:48,980
weekly or monthly reports.

55
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:54,565
For Naledi, Home shows what needs
attention across every farm:

56
00:03:54,605 --> 00:03:57,994
new requests, quiet kits and
farmers without Telegram.

57
00:03:58,034 --> 00:04:04,421
Every action is logged, so a small team can
look after many farms without losing

58
00:04:04,461 --> 00:04:04,850
track.

59
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:08,427
We tested as we built.

60
00:04:08,467 --> 00:04:15,259
Forms reject bad input, like a wrong phone
number or a run over 60 minutes.

61
00:04:15,299 --> 00:04:21,635
In our local test runs on 9 and 10
October, all 1,301 backend tests,

62
00:04:21,675 --> 00:04:26,190
all 112 admin tests and all 64
mobile tests passed.

63
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:28,834
AgroFlow recommends.

64
00:04:28,874 --> 00:04:30,550
The farmer decides.

65
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:34,000
Every number traces back to its source.

66
00:04:34,490 --> 00:04:38,520
Built by Team 2 for INF3003W.

67
00:04:39,010 --> 00:04:40,680
Thank you for watching.
